## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design simple concurrent systems with cancellation semantics, ordering guarantees, and backpressure within a bounded queue.

## Key Concepts

- Cancellation tokens attached to tasks
- Per-service FIFO buffers
- Global bounded work queue
- Worker coordination and cancellation checks
- Backpressure and graceful shutdown

## Code Example

```go
type Event struct {
  Data   string
  Cancel <-chan struct{}
}

func worker(id int, queue <-chan Event, done <-chan struct{}) {
  for {
    select {
    case e := <-queue:
      select {
      case <-e.Cancel:
        // canceled before processing
        continue
      default:
        process(e)
      }
    case <-done:
      return
    }
  }
}
```

